<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Menelaus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">In Greek mythology, Menelaus was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, the brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agamemnon">Agamemnon</a> and husband of Helen. When Helen left with the Trojan prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, he and Agamemnon led the Greek expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a> he is shown back in Sparta, reconciled with Helen, and he was honoured with her at the Menelaion near Sparta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/menelaus.jpg" alt="Menelaus" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giacomo Brogi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brogi,_Giacomo_(1822-1881)_-_n._4140_-_Roma_-_Vaticano_-_Menelao_-_Busto_in_marmo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
